# Files below /opt/dsf/sd that belong to the machine, not to the image.
#
# Everything the image ships under a slot-shared path is pushed back over the
# device's copy on every boot, which is what keeps the printer configuration in
# step with the installed version. The paths listed here must not take part in
# that: they hold per-machine and per-material tuning that a customer or a
# calibration run produced. They are moved out of the image into
# /usr/share/meltingplot/dsf-skel and seeded once by mp-dsf-seed, so they are
# created if missing and never touched again. The same globs keep the files
# out of the line-number/CRC pass.
#
# The list matches the protected files of the MeltingplotConfig DWC plugin.
# Paths are relative to /opt/dsf/sd and may contain shell globs.
#
# From chx350-config 3.7 on, everything machine-owned sits in two directories,
# so a new machine-owned file needs no entry here:
#   sys/overrides/   what the operator edits: global-override.g,
#                    machine-override, dsf-config-override.g and the printer
#                    name (printer-name.g, written by mp-dsf-seed and
#                    mp-set-printer-name, loaded last by dsf-config.g)
#   sys/generated/   what the machine writes about itself (nozzle, spool,
#                    filament diameter, bed surface, last filament
#                    temperature); the image never ships these
#
# Not listed, because the machine writes them and the image never ships them:
# sys/meltingplot/z-probe/szp_*_calibration_*.g, sys/heightmap.csv,
# sys/dwc-settings.json, filaments/*/config-auto-*.g

sys/config-override.g
sys/overrides/*
sys/generated/*
filaments/*/config-override.g
filaments/*/temps.g
filaments/*/material.g
filaments/*/nozzle-*.g

# pre-3.7 layout of chx350-config (the override files next to the system
# macros). Kept until the pinned submodule has moved on; with a 3.7
# configuration these match nothing.
sys/meltingplot/machine-override
sys/meltingplot/dsf-config-override.g
sys/meltingplot/global-override.g
sys/meltingplot/printer-name.g
